		(uuid "0ac74439-c4ad-5a28-9e7b-6e486351e7ef")
	)
	(text "NOTES:\n\n  - Both regulators are LM5164DDAR at approximately 300 kHz with 100 µH inductors.\n  - The +12 V rail follows TI's 12 V / 1 A Type-3 network except for the qualified 100 µH inductor.\n  - +3V3 reuses carrier's schematic.\n  - Input ceramics are rated for 100 V.\n  - Each rail uses two 22 µF / 25 V output capacitors.\n\nTODO:\n\n  - [ ] Verify VIN ringing at each regulator, output ripple, PGOOD inductor temperature, and fan startup/stall.\n\nLAYOUT:\n\n  - Place input ceramics directly at each regulator's VIN/GND pins with a minimum-area loop.\n  - Place L1/L2 close to SW and minimize the SW copper area.\n  - Place C4/C14 at L1's output and C10/C11 at L2's output; return each pair directly to regulator GND/EP.\n  - Keep feedback and ripple-injection parts close to FB and away from SW."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14.986 51.816 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.143 1.143)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "4a96cb1d-0573-596c-af4e-a99d5f050705")
	)
